    "TENANT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 15.129,
   "end": 18.129,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "THE CASE IS ABOUT",
    "A PIECE OF PAPER."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "A PIECE OF PAPER"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 29.061,
   "end": 35.061,
   "kind": "acttitle",
   "title": "THE LADDER AS WRITTEN",
   "kicker": "ACT ONE",
   "index": 1
  },
  {
   "start": 50.46,
   "end": 56.46,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "LINNIE LINDSEY · BARBARA HODGENS · PAMELA RAY",
   "secondary": "Tenants in a Louisville housing project, 1975. Named once in the opinion, and not again."
  },
  {
   "start": 71.859,
   "end": 77.859,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "ONCE THE PAPER WAS ON THE DOOR,",
    "THE TENANT HAD BEEN SERVED."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "HAD BEEN SERVED"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 93.258,
   "end": 99.258,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "FORCIBLE ENTRY AND DETAINER",
   "secondary": "The summary process a landlord uses to get possession back quickly. Speed is the point of it."
  },
  {
   "start": 114.657,
   "end": 120.657,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "JOSEPH GREENE",
   "secondary": "Jefferson County Sheriff. His deputies carried the writs."
  },
  {
   "start": 136.056,
   "end": 142.056,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "USUALLY A DEPUTY.",
    "UNNAMED IN THE CAPTION."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "UNNAMED"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 157.455,
   "end": 163.455,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "THEIR LANDLORD",
    "WAS NOT A LANDLORD."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "NOT A LANDLORD"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 178.854,
   "end": 184.854,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "THE QUESTION PRESENTED",
   "secondary": "Whether the statute, as applied to tenants in a public housing project, fails to afford them the notice the Fourteenth Amendment requires"
  },
  {
   "start": 200.254,
   "end": 206.254,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "A HEARING YOU DO NOT KNOW ABOUT",
    "IS NOT A HEARING",
    "YOU FAILED TO ATTEND."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "YOU FAILED TO ATTEND"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 221.653,
   "end": 227.653,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "The fundamental requisite of due process of law is the opportunity to be heard.",
   "attribution": "Grannis v. Ordean (1914), quoted in Greene v. Lindsey"
  },
  {
   "start": 243.052,
   "end": 249.052,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "little reality or worth unless one is informed that the matter is pending and can choose for himself whether to appear or default, acquiesce or contest",
   "attribution": "Mullane v. Central Hanover Bank & Trust (1950), quoted in Greene v. Lindsey"
  },
  {
   "start": 264.451,
   "end": 270.451,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "SECTION 454.030",
   "secondary": "Two sentences. Almost everything turns on the order of the clauses."
  },
  {
   "start": 285.85,
   "end": 291.85,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "FIND THE PERSON.",
    "FAILING THAT, THE HOUSEHOLD.",
    "FAILING THAT, THE DOOR."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "THE DOOR"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 307.249,
   "end": 313.249,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "SOMEBODY HOME.",
    "SOMEBODY OLD ENOUGH",
    "TO PASS IT ON."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "SOMEBODY HOME"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 328.648,
   "end": 334.648,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "THE NOTICE SHALL STATE THE TIME AND PLACE OF MEETING OF THE COURT",
   "secondary": "The shortest sentence in the statute, and the reason the paper exists"
  },
  {
   "start": 350.047,
   "end": 356.047,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "FOR ALL THREE OF THEM",
    "IT WENT ALL THE WAY DOWN."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "ALL THE WAY DOWN"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 371.446,
   "end": 377.446,
   "kind": "stat",
   "value": 0,
   "label": "Conversations on a doorstep, across all three apartments"
  },
  {
   "start": 398.323,
   "end": 404.323,
   "kind": "acttitle",
   "title": "ONE RUNG",
   "kicker": "ACT TWO",
   "index": 2
  },
  {
   "start": 411.678,
   "end": 417.678,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "Posting refers to the practice of placing the writ on the property by use of a thumbtack, adhesive tape, or other means.",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey, 456 U.S. 444 (1982), n. 1 — defining the term"
  },
  {
   "start": 425.032,
   "end": 431.032,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "THE SHERIFF'S OWN SEQUENCE",
   "secondary": "Personal service · a family member over sixteen · posting"
  },
  {
   "start": 438.386,
   "end": 444.386,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "IF NO ONE ANSWERS THE DOOR,",
    "A COPY IS POSTED",
    "ON THE PREMISES."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "ON THE PREMISES"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 451.74,
   "end": 457.74,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "But if no one is at home at the time of that visit, as is apparently true in a good percentage of cases, posting follows forthwith.",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey (1982) — the Court's own sentence; \"good percentage\" is quoted from a deposition, n. 8"
  },
  {
   "start": 465.095,
   "end": 471.095,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "FORTHWITH.",
    "THE SAME VISIT."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "THE SAME VISIT"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 478.449,
   "end": 484.449,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "Neither the statute, nor the practice of the process servers, makes provision for even a second attempt at personal service, perhaps at some time of day when the tenant is more likely to be at home.",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey (1982)"
  },
  {
   "start": 491.803,
   "end": 497.803,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "we reject appellants' characterization of the procedure",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey (1982)"
  },
  {
   "start": 505.158,
   "end": 511.158,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "THE LADDER",
    "HAD ONE RUNG."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "ONE RUNG"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 518.512,
   "end": 524.512,
   "kind": "highlightring",
   "cx": 0.5,
   "cy": 0.52,
   "r": 0.13,
   "label": "\"a good percentage\" — quoted from a deposition, not the Court's own estimate"
  },
  {
   "start": 531.866,
   "end": 537.866,
   "kind": "mechanism",
   "mechanism": "gears"
  },
  {
   "start": 545.221,
   "end": 551.221,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "a singularly appropriate and effective way of ensuring that a person who cannot conveniently be served personally is actually apprised of proceedings against him",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey (1982), on what posting is in most cases"
  },
  {
   "start": 558.575,
   "end": 564.575,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "SINGULARLY APPROPRIATE",
    "AND EFFECTIVE."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "AND EFFECTIVE"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 571.929,
   "end": 577.929,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "It is, of course, reasonable to assume that a property owner will maintain superintendence of his property",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey (1982), restating why posting normally works"
  },
  {
   "start": 585.284,
   "end": 591.284,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "DID THE PAPER STAY UP",
    "LONG ENOUGH TO BE READ?"
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "LONG ENOUGH"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 610.447,
   "end": 616.447,
   "kind": "acttitle",
   "title": "WELL AWARE",
   "kicker": "ACT THREE",
   "index": 3
  },
  {
   "start": 628.419,
   "end": 634.419,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "Oh, we had plenty of trouble.",
   "attribution": "A process server, under oath, asked about children ripping the writs off — Greene v. Lindsey, n. 7"
  },
  {
   "start": 646.391,
   "end": 652.391,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "I have seen them take them off of the door and I would go back and tell them to put it back. They don't know.",
   "attribution": "The same deposition excerpt, n. 7"
  },
  {
   "start": 664.363,
   "end": 670.363,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "VILLAGE WEST",
   "secondary": "Named twice in the same footnote. The dissent gives the man who said \"probably a couple of times\" a name: Carter Bacon."
  },
  {
   "start": 682.336,
   "end": 688.336,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "the Housing Authority told us that they would take them off, so we always put them up high",
   "attribution": "A third deposition excerpt in the same footnote (App. 74)"
  },
  {
   "start": 700.308,
   "end": 706.308,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "THE HOUSING AUTHORITY",
    "TOLD US."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "TOLD US"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 718.28,
   "end": 724.28,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "As the process servers were well aware, notices posted on apartment doors in the area where these tenants lived were not infrequently removed by children or other tenants before they could have their intended effect.",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey, 456 U.S. 444 (1982)"
  },
  {
   "start": 736.252,
   "end": 742.252,
   "kind": "stat",
   "value": 0,
   "label": "Studies, surveys or counts the majority weighed against the depositions"
  },
  {
   "start": 754.224,
   "end": 760.224,
   "kind": "spotlight",
   "cx": 0.5,
   "cy": 0.5,
   "r": 0.19,
   "dim": 0.74
  },
  {
   "start": 772.196,
   "end": 778.196,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "and the six months I was working at it there was no occasion where I saw anyone tear the Writs off of the door",
   "attribution": "A process server, quoted only in the dissent"
  },
  {
   "start": 790.168,
   "end": 796.168,
   "kind": "lowerthird",
   "primary": "GILBERT BRUTSCHER",
   "secondary": "Same job, opposite answer. The dissent does not say they worked the same buildings."
  },
  {
   "start": 808.14,
   "end": 814.14,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "we always try to put the paper up above where, a, say a small child can't reach it",
   "attribution": "Another process server, quoted in the dissent"
  },
  {
   "start": 826.113,
   "end": 832.113,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "THE MAJORITY QUOTED",
    "THE FIRST HALF.",
    "THE DISSENT QUOTED",
    "THE SECOND."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "THE SECOND"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 844.085,
   "end": 850.085,
   "kind": "quote",
   "quote": "claim never to have seen these posted summonses; they state that they did not learn of the eviction proceedings until they were served with writs of possession",
   "attribution": "Greene v. Lindsey (1982), Part I — the appellees' allegation"
  },
  {
   "start": 862.057,
   "end": 868.057,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "CLAIM. STATE.",
    "NOT DID SUFFER."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
    "NOT DID SUFFER"
   ]
  },
  {
   "start": 880.029,
   "end": 886.029,
   "kind": "kinetic",
   "lines": [
    "NOBODY EVER TRIED",
    "THAT QUESTION."
   ],
   "style": "emphasis",
   "emphasisWords": [
